6. Learning and Consolidation Dynamics

6.1 Fast Weights with Spectral Regularization

For each expert i,

\theta_i(t+1)
=
\theta_i(t)
-
\eta_i(t)
\nabla_{\theta_i}
\left[
\tilde p_i(t)\,
\ell\!\left(o_t,f_{\bar\theta_i}(x_t,a_t)\right)
+
\lambda_{\mathrm{SPHERE}}\mathcal L_{\mathrm{spec},i}
\right],

where

\bar\theta_i(t)
=
\alpha_i^{\mathrm{fast}}(t)\theta_i(t)
+
\alpha_i^{\mathrm{slow}}(t)\phi_i(t).

The spectral regularizer is

\mathcal L_{\mathrm{spec},i}
=
\sum_{l=1}^{L_i}
\left\|
W_{i,l}^\top W_{i,l}-I
\right\|_F^2.

This maintains the effective rank of the neural tangent kernel.

6.2 Effective Rank

Let \mathbf K_t be the neural tangent kernel of the active fast weights. Let \sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_n be its singular values, and

p_k=\frac{\sigma_k}{\sum_j\sigma_j}.

The effective rank is

r_e(\mathbf K_t)
=
\exp\!\left(
-\sum_{k=1}^{n}p_k\log p_k
\right).

We enforce

r_e(\mathbf K_t)\ge r_{\min}

by increasing \lambda_{\mathrm{SPHERE}} when the effective rank falls.

6.3 Slow Weights

\phi_i(t+1)
=
\beta_i(t)\phi_i(t)
+
(1-\beta_i(t))\theta_i(t).

6.4 Inter-Expert Communication

w_{ij}(t+1)
=
w_{ij}(t)
+
\eta_{ij}(m_t)
\left[
\tilde p_i(t)\tilde p_j(t)\,z_i^\top z_j
-
\lambda w_{ij}(t)
\right],

with

\eta_{ij}(m_t)
=
\eta_{\max}
\sigma\!\left(\omega_{ij}^\top m_t\right).

---

7. Structural Adaptation

Structural expansion follows a probe-based singular-value energy criterion.

7.1 Probe-Based Novel Subspace Estimation

For an incoming data window \mathcal D_k, fit a probe LoRA adapter A_{\mathrm{probe}} of rank r_{\max} for N_{\mathrm{probe}} steps, keeping historical adapters frozen.

Let the historical basis be

A_{\mathrm{hist}}
=
\mathrm{Concat}\!\left(A_1,\dots,A_{M_{k-1}}\right),

and compute its QR decomposition

Q_{\mathrm{hist}}=\mathrm{QR}(A_{\mathrm{hist}}).

Define the residual

A_{\mathrm{diff}}
=
A_{\mathrm{probe}}
\left(
I-Q_{\mathrm{hist}}^\top Q_{\mathrm{hist}}
\right).

Compute the singular value decomposition

A_{\mathrm{diff}}
=
U\Sigma V^\top,
\qquad
\Sigma=\mathrm{diag}(\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_{r_{\max}}).

The novel rank r_{\mathrm{new}} is the smallest integer r such that

\frac{
\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_i^2
}{
\sum_{j=1}^{r_{\max}}\sigma_j^2
}
\ge
\theta_{\mathrm{energy}},

with \theta_{\mathrm{energy}}=0.9.

7.2 Creation Gate

A new expert is created if and only if:

1. r_{\mathrm{new}}>0,
2. \min_i\epsilon_i(t)>\tau_C for \tau_{\mathrm{create}} consecutive steps,
3. \|\nabla_\theta e_t\|<\delta,
4. B(\mathcal G_t)+\mathrm{cost}(r_{\mathrm{new}})\le B_{\max}.

Here

\epsilon_i(t)
=
\|o_t-f_{\bar\theta_i}(x_t,a_t)\|_{\Sigma^{-1}}^2

and

B(\mathcal G_t)=\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}c_i.

The new expert is initialized with rank r_{\mathrm{new}} and prototype v_{\mathrm{new}}=u_t/(\|u_t\|+\varepsilon).

7.3 Pruning

Expert i is removed if

q_i(t)<\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}

for T_{\mathrm{prune}} consecutive steps. Competence updates as

q_i(t+1)
=
\mathrm{clip}_{[0,1]}\!\left(
(1-\alpha_q)q_i(t)
+
\alpha_q\tilde p_i(t)\exp(-\epsilon_i(t))
\right).

