Appendix B. Proof of Lemma 1: Queue Drift Bound

Lemma 1. Let the compute queues Q_j(t) and plasticity queues P_i(t) evolve according to

Q_j(t+1)=\max\{0,\ Q_j(t)+\kappa_j(t)-\bar\kappa_j\},

P_i(t+1)=\max\{0,\ P_i(t)+\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2-\delta_i^{\max}\}.

Assume that \kappa_j(t) is bounded by \kappa_j^{\max} and \|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2 is bounded by \Delta_i^{\max} for all t. Define

\mathcal L_Q(t)=\frac12\sum_{j=1}^{N_r}Q_j(t)^2+\frac12\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}P_i(t)^2.

Then there exists a constant C>0 such that

\Delta\mathcal L_Q(t)\le C-\sum_{j=1}^{N_r}Q_j(t)\bigl(\bar\kappa_j-\kappa_j(t)\bigr)-\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}P_i(t)\bigl(\delta_i^{\max}-\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2\bigr).

Proof. For any scalar queue

Q(t+1)=\max\{0,Q(t)+a(t)-b\},

we have the elementary inequality

\max\{0,x\}^2\le x^2.

Applying this with x=Q(t)+a(t)-b,

Q(t+1)^2
\le
\bigl(Q(t)+a(t)-b\bigr)^2
=
Q(t)^2+2Q(t)(a(t)-b)+(a(t)-b)^2.

Rearranging,

\frac12 Q(t+1)^2-\frac12 Q(t)^2
\le
Q(t)(a(t)-b)+\frac12(a(t)-b)^2.

For each compute queue, a(t)=\kappa_j(t), b=\bar\kappa_j. Thus

\frac12 Q_j(t+1)^2-\frac12 Q_j(t)^2
\le
Q_j(t)(\kappa_j(t)-\bar\kappa_j)
+
\frac12(\kappa_j(t)-\bar\kappa_j)^2.

For each plasticity queue, a(t)=\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2, b=\delta_i^{\max}. Hence

\frac12 P_i(t+1)^2-\frac12 P_i(t)^2
\le
P_i(t)\bigl(\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2-\delta_i^{\max}\bigr)
+
\frac12\bigl(\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2-\delta_i^{\max}\bigr)^2.

Summing over j and i,

\Delta\mathcal L_Q(t)
\le
\sum_{j=1}^{N_r}Q_j(t)(\kappa_j(t)-\bar\kappa_j)
+
\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}P_i(t)\bigl(\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2-\delta_i^{\max}\bigr)
+
C(t),

where

C(t)=
\frac12\sum_{j=1}^{N_r}(\kappa_j(t)-\bar\kappa_j)^2
+
\frac12\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}\bigl(\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2-\delta_i^{\max}\bigr)^2.

Under boundedness assumptions, there exists a constant C independent of t such that C(t)\le C. Multiplying the drift inequality by -1 on the terms inside yields

\Delta\mathcal L_Q(t)
\le
C
-
\sum_{j=1}^{N_r}Q_j(t)\bigl(\bar\kappa_j-\kappa_j(t)\bigr)
-
\sum_{i=1}^{M_t}P_i(t)\bigl(\delta_i^{\max}-\|\theta_i(t+1)-\theta_i(t)\|^2\bigr).

This completes the proof.

