Appendix I. Statement of Assumptions and Limitations

All theoretical results depend on assumptions (A1)–(A6), which may not hold in arbitrary deep networks. In particular, strong convexity of local losses is a local approximation. The small-gain condition requires estimating gains, which is difficult in practice. The present manuscript provides a theoretical scaffold; empirical validation is left to future work. No simulations, code training, or physical experiments have been conducted.

